{"id":"11b61659960c0df8","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-brouwer-degrees.md","title":"Brouwer Degree","display":"df-brouwer-degrees — Brouwer Degree","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-brouwer-degrees","aliases":["58-df-brouwer-degrees"],"display":"df-brouwer-degrees — Brouwer Degree","depends_on":["[[58-df-smooth-map]]","[[58-df-orientation]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-brouwer-degrees"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-brouwer-degrees</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-brouwer-degrees — Brouwer Degree"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d87c5d842ade903d\" href=\"?note=d87c5d842ade903d\" title=\"58-df-smooth-map\">58-df-smooth-map</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bc8c800bbf59f617\" href=\"?note=bc8c800bbf59f617\" title=\"58-df-orientation\">58-df-orientation</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\">\\(n\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\\)</span> (dimension)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{OrientedBoundedDomain}_S(B,n)\">\\(\\operatorname{OrientedBoundedDomain}_S(B,n)\\)</span> (oriented bounded-domain predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bc8c800bbf59f617\" href=\"?note=bc8c800bbf59f617\" title=\"58-df-orientation\">58-df-orientation</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f:\\overline B\\to\\mathbb R^n\">\\(f:\\overline B\\to\\mathbb R^n\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C^1\">\\(C^1\\)</span> map, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"d87c5d842ade903d\" href=\"?note=d87c5d842ade903d\" title=\"58-df-smooth-map\">58-df-smooth-map</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"y\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus f[\\partial B]\">\\(y\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus f[\\partial B]\\)</span> (value away from the boundary image)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Df(x)\">\\(Df(x)\\)</span> (Jacobian derivative)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{sgn}\">\\(\\operatorname{sgn}\\)</span> (sign function)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d_B\\in\\mathbb Z\">\\(d_B\\in\\mathbb Z\\)</span> (candidate value of the regular-value degree formula)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularValueBrouwerDegree}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularValueBrouwerDegree}_S\\)</span> (regular-value Brouwer-degree relation defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brouwer-degrees} \\vdash \\mathrm{RegularValueBrouwerDegree}_S(d_B,f,B,y,n)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{OrientedBoundedDomain}_S(B,n)\\land f\\in C^1(\\overline B,\\mathbb R^n)\\land y\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus f[\\partial B]\\land\\forall x\\in B\\;(f(x)=y\\to\\det Df(x)\\neq0)\\land d_B=\\sum_{x\\in B\\cap f^{-1}[\\{y\\}]}\\operatorname{sgn}(\\det Df(x))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brouwer-degrees} \\vdash \\mathrm{RegularValueBrouwerDegree}_S(d_B,f,B,y,n)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{OrientedBoundedDomain}_S(B,n)\\land f\\in C^1(\\overline B,\\mathbb R^n)\\land y\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus f[\\partial B]\\land\\forall x\\in B\\;(f(x)=y\\to\\det Df(x)\\neq0)\\land d_B=\\sum_{x\\in B\\cap f^{-1}[\\{y\\}]}\\operatorname{sgn}(\\det Df(x))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Brouwer degree is invariant under homotopies that keep <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"y\">\\(y\\)</span> outside the image of the boundary.</li>\n<li>The displayed signed-Jacobian sum is the regular-value formula; the general degree is obtained by homotopy/approximation.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-smooth-map","status":"resolved","id":"d87c5d842ade903d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-smooth-map]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-orientation","status":"resolved","id":"bc8c800bbf59f617","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-orientation]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-orientation","status":"resolved","id":"bc8c800bbf59f617","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{OrientedBoundedDomain}_S(B,n)$ (oriented bounded-domain predicate, see [[58-df-orientation]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-smooth-map","status":"resolved","id":"d87c5d842ade903d","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$f:\\overline B\\to\\mathbb R^n$ ($C^1$ map, see [[58-df-smooth-map]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\omega_{>0}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{OrientedBoundedDomain}_S(B,n)","display":false},{"tex":"f:\\overline B\\to\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"C^1","display":false},{"tex":"y\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus f[\\partial B]","display":false},{"tex":"Df(x)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{sgn}","display":false},{"tex":"d_B\\in\\mathbb Z","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularValueBrouwerDegree}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brouwer-degrees} \\vdash \\mathrm{RegularValueBrouwerDegree}_S(d_B,f,B,y,n)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{OrientedBoundedDomain}_S(B,n)\\land f\\in C^1(\\overline B,\\mathbb R^n)\\land y\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus f[\\partial B]\\